    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1896-98/document/175> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420766261/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """mourners, and a more cordial farewell to Miss Paget, we came away. 
Edith was curiously impressed by the sight of these maiden ladies, dressed in stiff shirt-fronts with wrinkles where most women have a certain fulness, crossing their legs and putting their hands in their pockets, and taking this petty little squabble with the seriousness of a European war at least. She felt a MAN was needed in that atmosphere to give them a little sense of real values!! 
I liked Miss Paget better than before, and my bad opinion of Miss Thomson was deepened. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 175 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1896-98> .

